                "word": "pommage",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a50b709d-51ec-30b9-8df3-b86f70ebc944",
                        "entry_id": "bb22dedf-97bb-3b74-a5f0-53c308e9622a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The set of apple and/or pear varieties grown in a region or location."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0e40df4-d8be-4bbf-b565-8bcaaec08d8c",
                                "sense_id": "a50b709d-51ec-30b9-8df3-b86f70ebc944",
                                "text": "In a certain locality, however, it is not all the varieties included in the regional pommage that are traditionally grown, and that locality might have a pommage which is a subset of the regionl one."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "52ef265b-8bb3-373b-b05b-3eb97e157105",
                        "entry_id": "bb22dedf-97bb-3b74-a5f0-53c308e9622a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The ground-up apples from which cider is pressed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7efb9493-93fc-41df-9ab3-a32675d84664",
                                "sense_id": "52ef265b-8bb3-373b-b05b-3eb97e157105",
                                "text": "In grinding the apples for this use into pommage, several methods are practised; but the two most chiefly in use are, the bruising-stone with a circular trough, and the apple-mill."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ee49e8a-9f2d-4e93-aac7-99abe22655c1",
                                "sense_id": "52ef265b-8bb3-373b-b05b-3eb97e157105",
                                "text": "This is effected by placing clear sweet straw, or hair cloths, between the layers of pommage, till there is a pile of ten or twelve layers. This pile is then subjected to different degrees of pressure in succession, till all the must or juice is squeezed from the pommage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d5427db-c988-4d97-9145-93025a49a1fa",
                                "sense_id": "52ef265b-8bb3-373b-b05b-3eb97e157105",
                                "text": "After the apples are gathered from the trees, they are ground into what is called pommage, either by means of a common pressing stone, with a circular trough, or by a cider mill, which is either driven by hand or by horse power."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53a0982f-4a9d-3a28-be40-e25e734042b0",
